# HFSM library (`core/lib/hfsm`)

Port of Library `GDScript/HFSM` / `Python3/HFSM`. Keep semantics in sync; do not invent parallel FSM APIs here.

## Modules

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `state_node.gd` / `state_tree.gd` | Config data only — no live entities |
| `loader.gd` | JSON/dict → tree; reserved keys: `enter`, `leave`, `consume`, `states` |
| `hfsm.gd` | Queue, transitions, `sys.enter` propagation |
| `binding_registry.gd` | Entity lifecycle; instances by `state.name` → `{slot: entity}` |
| `bound_entity.gd` | Base: `const NAME`, `on_event`, `deinit` |
| `event.gd` / `utils.gd` / `consts.gd` | Event + pattern helpers |

## Public API

- `HFSM.new(tree, entities)` — `entities`: `{ slot: { EntityNAME: Script } }`
- `HfsmLoader.load_tree(path|Dictionary)` / `try_load_tree` (errors without throw)
- `add_event(name, data)`, `get_active_path()`, `get_binding(state, slot)`, `reset()`

## Transition semantics (do not change casually)

- Post-order: children processed before parent
- `leave` → deactivate subtree + `entity.deinit()`
- Matching child `enter` → activate + `on_enter` + entity `on_event` (except `sys.enter`)
- `consume`: stop bubble **unless** event also matches this state's enter/leave
- `sys.enter`: no entity `on_event`; used for default child activation
- Auto-activate child only if `enter` is **exactly** `["sys.enter"]` (omitted `enter` in JSON → that)
- If parent active and **no** active child → activate all pure-`sys.enter` children
- Wildcard `*` only at **end** of pattern (`ev.ui_*`)

## Entities

- Subclass `HfsmBoundEntity`; define `const NAME = "..."` matching JSON binding value
- Registry key must equal `NAME` (registry indexes by script `NAME`)
- `on_enter` constructs `script.new(event_data)`; `on_leave` calls `deinit()`
- Machine must not instantiate entities outside `HfsmBindingRegistry`

## Must / avoid

- Keep library project-agnostic (no Quizmatik types in `core/lib/hfsm`)
- Behavior change → add/adjust tests (Library suite is the reference)
- Avoid Godot nodes inside the lib — `RefCounted` only
